Notebook[
 {
  Cell[
   "Lepton-quark scattering, step 2 (FeynCalc route): spin and colour \
algebra", "Title"], Cell["Input: Results/Amplitudes.wl from step 1.  Output: \
Results/FeynCalc/Algebra.wl, the squared matrix elements as scalar functions \
of the invariants, for the spin average (\"Unpolarized\") and the incoming \
double-helicity difference (\"Polarized\").  Step 3 reads either route's \
Algebra.wl; the three routes must agree here.\n\nConventions.  Massless \
kinematics with s = 2 l.k, t = -2 k.p, u = -2 l.p.  For real emission the \
extra invariants are a = (k - r)^2 = -2 k.r, b = (p + r)^2 = 2 p.r, tau = (k \
- p - r)^2 = a + b + t (photon virtuality) and s4 = (lp + r)^2 = s + t + u.  \
Dimensional regularization with D = 4 - 2 eps.\n\nSpin.  The spin average is \
1/2 per incoming fermion, the colour average 1/Nc for the quark; final spins \
and colours are summed.  The double-longitudinal difference Delta sigma = \
(sigma(++) - sigma(+-))/2 is obtained by replacing the density matrix \
p-slash/2 of each incoming fermion by p-slash gamma5/2; gamma5 is treated in \
the HVBM (BMHV) scheme, in which the external momenta l, k, p are \
four-dimensional while the unobserved momenta lp, r and the loop momentum \
keep their (D-4)-dimensional (\"hatted\") components.  spe3 denotes the \
hatted invariant rhat.rhat = lphat.lphat = -lphat.rhat of the unobserved \
pair.", "Text"], Cell["Load", "Section"], Cell["The package must be loaded in \
a cell of its own, before any cell that uses its functions is parsed.", 
   "Text"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \
\"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], Cell["LoadFeynCalc[];\namplitu\
des = LoadAmplitudes[][\"FeynCalc\"];\nKeys[amplitudes]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Born: l q -> l q", "Section"], Cell["Unpolarized square: sum over the \
two fermion lines with FermionSpinSum, average 1/4 over the incoming spins \
and 1/Nc over the incoming quark colour.  The D-dimensional result keeps its \
(D-4) term, which multiplies collinear poles later.", "Text"], 
  Cell["FCClearScalarProducts[];\nSetMandelstam[s, t, u, l, k, -lp, -p, 0, 0, \
0, 0];\nbornAmplitude = Total[amplitudes[\"Born\"]];\nbornUnpolarized = \
bornAmplitude ComplexConjugate[bornAmplitude]/SUNN //\n  \
FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit // SUNSimplify[#, Explicit -> True] & //\n  \
FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor -> 1/4] & // DiracSimplify[#, \
DiracTraceEvaluate -> True] & //\n  Contract // TrickMandelstam[#, {s, t, u, \
0}] & // Factor;\nbornUnpolarized = bornUnpolarized /. {SMP[\"e\"] -> ee, \
SMP[\"g_s\"] -> gs}", "Input"], Cell["Expected: 2 ee^4 eq^2 ((s^2 + u^2)/t^2 \
- eps) with D = 4 - 2 eps (TrickMandelstam has used s + t + u = 0, which \
holds for the 2 -> 2 kinematics).", "Text"], Cell["Require[Simplify[(bornUnpo\
larized - 2 ee^4 eq^2 ((s^2 + u^2)/t^2 - (4 - D)/2)) /. u -> -s - t] === 0, \
\"Born square differs from the textbook result\"];", "Input"], 
  Cell["Helicity difference.  FeynCalc's FermionSpinSum inserts p-slash for \
every spinor; to get p-slash gamma5 for the two incoming fermions we \
temporarily rename their momenta (lHel, kHel) and replace the slashes it \
produces by GSD[l].GA[5] and GSD[k].GA[5].  FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"] \
selects the HVBM scheme; $LeviCivitaSign = -1 fixes Tr[gamma^a gamma^b \
gamma^c gamma^d gamma5] = -4 i eps^{abcd}, the convention in which Tracer and \
FORM below are written.  Momentum[x, D-4] = 0 declares x four-dimensional.", 
   "Text"], Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"];\n$LeviCivitaSign = \
-1;\nFCClearScalarProducts[];\nSetMandelstam[s, t, u, l, k, -lp, -p, 0, 0, 0, \
0];\nScan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {l, k, lp, p}];\nhelicityTag = \
{Spinor[Momentum[l, D], m_, o_] :> Spinor[Momentum[lHel, D], m, o],\n  \
Spinor[Momentum[k, D], m_, o_] :> Spinor[Momentum[kHel, D], m, \
o]};\nhelicityDensity = {DiracGamma[Momentum[lHel, D], D] :> GSD[l].GA[5],\n  \
DiracGamma[Momentum[kHel, D], D] :> GSD[k].GA[5]};\nbornPolarized = \
(bornAmplitude ComplexConjugate[bornAmplitude]/SUNN /. helicityTag) //\n  \
FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit // SUNSimplify[#, Explicit -> True] & //\n  \
FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor -> 1/4] & // ReplaceAll[#, helicityDensity] & \
//\n  DiracSimplify[#, DiracTraceEvaluate -> True] & // Contract // \
ExpandScalarProduct //\n  TrickMandelstam[Cancel[Together[#]], {s, t, u, 0}] \
& // Factor;\nbornPolarized = bornPolarized /. {SMP[\"e\"] -> ee, \
SMP[\"g_s\"] -> gs}", "Input"], 
  Cell["Expected: 2 ee^4 eq^2 (s^2 - u^2)/t^2, with no (D-4) term.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Require[Simplify[(bornPolarized - 2 ee^4 eq^2 (s^2 - u^2)/t^2) /. u \
-> -s - t] === 0, \"Polarized Born square differs from the expected \
result\"];\nborn = <|\"Unpolarized\" -> bornUnpolarized, \"Polarized\" -> \
bornPolarized|>;", "Input"], Cell["Virtual: the one-loop vertex correction", 
   "Section"], Cell["The interference 2 Re(M_vertex M_Born^ of the vertex \
graph with the Born amplitude is a vector-current form factor times the Born \
square, so it is the same for both spin cases.  TID expresses the tensor loop \
integral through the scalar integrals B0 and C0 (Passarino-Veltman \
functions); dividing by the Born square leaves a scalar expression.  We write \
it in terms of the scalar integral family\n\n   VirtualIntegral[n0, n1, n2] = \
integral over the loop momentum of 1/((loop^2)^n0 ((loop-k)^2)^n1 \
((loop-p)^2)^n2),\n\nwhich Kira reduces to a single master integral in step \
3.  The on-shell bubble B0[0,0,0] is scaleless and vanishes; keeping it \
visible ($KeepLogDivergentScalelessIntegrals) documents where it would \
enter.", "Text"], Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"NDR\"];\nFCClearScalarProduct\
s[];\nSetMandelstam[s, t, u, l, k, -lp, -p, 0, 0, 0, \
0];\n$KeepLogDivergentScalelessIntegrals = True;\nvertexAmplitude = \
Total[amplitudes[\"VirtualVertex\"]] // DiracSimplify // Contract // \
SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] &;\nvertexScalar = vertexAmplitude // \
TID[#, loop, ToPaVe -> True] & // DiracSimplify // Contract //\n  \
SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] & // \
FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit;\nbornReduced = bornAmplitude // DiracSimplify // \
Contract // FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit;\nsquare[x_, y_] := x \
ComplexConjugate[y] // FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor -> 1/4] & // \
DiracSimplify //\n  SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] & // \
TrickMandelstam[#, {s, t, u, 0}] & // Simplify;\nvirtualRatio = \
Factor[square[2 vertexScalar, bornReduced]/square[bornReduced, bornReduced]]"\
, "Input"], Cell["The loop measure of TID is d^D loop/(2 pi)^D; the family is \
defined with measure d^D loop/(i pi^(D/2)), hence the factor 1/(2 CF Pi^2 \
gs^2) that also removes the colour factor CF and the coupling (the factor 2 \
is the 2 Re).  The master integral normalization is fixed in step 3.", 
   "Text"], Cell["virtualFamily = Factor[virtualRatio/(2 CF Pi^2 \
SMP[\"g_s\"]^2)] /. {\n  B0[0, 0, 0] -> VirtualIntegral[1, 1, 0], B0[t, 0, 0] \
-> VirtualIntegral[0, 1, 1],\n  C0[0, 0, t, 0, 0, 0] -> VirtualIntegral[1, 1, \
1]}", "Input"], Cell["Real emission: l q -> l q g", "Section"], 
  Cell["Unpolarized: square the sum of the two diagrams, sum the gluon \
polarizations with -g^{mu nu} (DoPolarizationSums with VirtualBoson -> True), \
average over spins and colour.  The five-particle kinematics is specified \
through all scalar products.", "Text"], Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"NDR\"];\
\nFCClearScalarProducts[];\nSPD[l] = 0; SPD[k] = 0; SPD[lp] = 0; SPD[p] = 0; \
SPD[r] = 0;\nSPD[l, k] = s/2; SPD[k, p] = -t/2; SPD[l, p] = -u/2; SPD[k, r] = \
-a/2; SPD[p, r] = b/2;\nSPD[l, lp] = -(a + b + t)/2; SPD[l, r] = (s + t + u + \
a + b)/2; SPD[k, lp] = (s + t + a)/2;\nSPD[lp, p] = -(t + u + b)/2; SPD[lp, \
r] = (s + t + u)/2;\nrealAmplitude = Total[SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] \
& /@ amplitudes[\"Real\"]] // DiracSimplify // Contract;\nrealUnpolarized = \
realAmplitude ComplexConjugate[realAmplitude]/SUNN // \
FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit //\n  SUNSimplify[#, Explicit -> True, SUNNToCACF \
-> True] & // FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor -> 1/4] & //\n  DiracSimplify // \
Contract // DoPolarizationSums[#, r, 0, VirtualBoson -> True] & // Contract \
// Simplify //\n  SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] & // \
Factor;\nrealUnpolarized = realUnpolarized /. {SMP[\"e\"] -> ee, SMP[\"g_s\"] \
-> gs}", "Input"], Cell["Helicity difference in the HVBM scheme.  Here l, k, \
p and the recoil momentum pRec = lp + r are four-dimensional, while lp and r \
individually have (D-4)-dimensional components with rhat.rhat = lphat.lphat = \
-lphat.rhat = spe3.  FeynCalc distinguishes D-dimensional products SPD, \
four-dimensional ones SP and (D-4)-dimensional ones SPE; all three are \
set.\n\nRather than the generic spin sum we write the two traces explicitly: \
the lepton trace Tr[lp-slash gamma^mu l-slash gamma5 gamma^nu]/2 and, for \
each pair (i, j) of the two quark currents, Tr[p-slash W_i k-slash gamma5 \
Wbar_j]/2, where W_1 = gamma^mu (k-slash - r-slash) gamma^rho and W_2 = \
gamma^rho (p-slash + r-slash) gamma^mu are the quark strings of the two \
diagrams (photon index mu, gluon index rho) and Wbar their reversed strings.  \
The factors 1/2 are the two helicity density matrices.  The photon indices \
mu, nu are four-dimensional (GA), the gluon indices D-dimensional (GAD); the \
gluon sum is -g_{rho sigma}.", "Text"], Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"]\
;\nFCClearScalarProducts[];\nScan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {l, k, p, \
pRec}];\nSPD[l] = 0; SPD[k] = 0; SPD[lp] = 0; SPD[p] = 0; SPD[r] = 0;\nSPD[l, \
k] = s/2; SPD[k, p] = -t/2; SPD[l, p] = -u/2; SPD[k, r] = -a/2; SPD[p, r] = \
b/2;\nSPD[l, lp] = -(a + b + t)/2; SPD[l, r] = (s + t + u + a + b)/2; SPD[k, \
lp] = (s + t + a)/2;\nSPD[lp, p] = -(t + u + b)/2; SPD[lp, r] = (s + t + \
u)/2;\nSPE[lp] = spe3; SPE[r] = spe3; SPE[lp, r] = -spe3;\nSP[l] = 0; SP[k] = \
0; SP[p] = 0; SP[lp] = -spe3; SP[r] = -spe3;\nSP[l, k] = s/2; SP[k, p] = \
-t/2; SP[l, p] = -u/2; SP[k, r] = -a/2; SP[p, r] = b/2;\nSP[l, lp] = -(a + b \
+ t)/2; SP[l, r] = (s + t + u + a + b)/2; SP[k, lp] = (s + t + a)/2;\nSP[lp, \
p] = -(t + u + b)/2; SP[lp, r] = (s + t + u)/2 + spe3;\nquarkStrings = \
{GA[mu].(GSD[k] - GSD[r]).GAD[rho], GAD[rho].(GSD[p] + \
GSD[r]).GA[mu]};\nquarkStringsBar = {GAD[sigma].(GSD[k] - GSD[r]).GA[nu], \
GA[nu].(GSD[p] + GSD[r]).GAD[sigma]};\nleptonTrace = \
DiracTrace[GSD[lp].GA[mu].GSD[l].GA[5].GA[nu]]/2;\nquarkTraces = \
Table[DiracTrace[GS[p].quarkStrings[[i]].GS[k].GA[5].quarkStringsBar[[j]]]/2, \
{i, 2}, {j, 2}];\ninterference = \
Table[Factor[Together[Simplify[Contract[ExpandScalarProduct[Contract[\n  \
DiracSimplify[leptonTrace quarkTraces[[i, j]], DiracTraceEvaluate -> True] \
(-MTD[rho, sigma])]]]]]], {i, 2}, {j, 2}];\nMatrixForm[interference]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Multiply by the propagators of the two diagrams, 1/(a tau) \
and 1/(b tau), the colour factor CF (from Tr[T^a T^a]/Nc), and the couplings \
ee^4 eq^2 gs^2 (the generated prefactors, 3 eq/2 times the charge 2/3 times \
i's, square to one).", "Text"], Cell["realPolarized = Factor[Together[CF ee^4 \
eq^2 gs^2/(a + b + t)^2 (\n  interference[[1, 1]]/a^2 + interference[[2, \
2]]/b^2 + (interference[[1, 2]] + interference[[2, 1]])/(a b))]];\nreal = \
<|\"Unpolarized\" -> realUnpolarized, \"Polarized\" -> \
realPolarized|>;\nFactor[realPolarized /. spe3 -> 0]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Photon-quark Born: gamma q -> q g", "Section"], 
  Cell["Needed through order eps for the photon-in-lepton subtraction.  \
Invariants sh = 2 q.k, th = -2 k.p, uh = -2 q.p.  Unpolarized: average 1/2 \
over the quark spin and 1/(D-2) over the photon polarizations, 1/Nc over \
colour.", "Text"], Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"NDR\"];\nFCClearScalarProduc\
ts[];\nSPD[q] = 0; SPD[k] = 0; SPD[p] = 0; SPD[r] = 0;\nSPD[q, k] = sh/2; \
SPD[k, p] = -th/2; SPD[q, p] = -uh/2; SPD[p, r] = sh/2; SPD[k, r] = -uh/2; \
SPD[q, r] = -th/2;\nphotonAmplitude = Total[SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> \
True] & /@ amplitudes[\"Photon\"]] // DiracSimplify // \
Contract;\nphotonUnpolarized = photonAmplitude \
ComplexConjugate[photonAmplitude]/SUNN // FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit //\n  \
SUNSimplify[#, Explicit -> True, SUNNToCACF -> True] & // FermionSpinSum[#, \
ExtraFactor -> 1/2] & //\n  DiracSimplify // Contract // \
DoPolarizationSums[#, r, 0, VirtualBoson -> True] & //\n  \
DoPolarizationSums[#, q, 0, VirtualBoson -> True] & // Contract // Simplify \
// SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] & // Factor;\nphotonUnpolarized = \
photonUnpolarized/(D - 2) /. {SMP[\"e\"] -> ee, SMP[\"g_s\"] -> gs}", 
   "Input"], Cell["Polarized: the circularly polarized photon has the density \
difference i eps^{mu nu q k}/(2 q.k) (with $LeviCivitaSign = -1) and the \
quark the density k-slash gamma5/2; all momenta of this 2 -> 2 process are \
four-dimensional, the final gluon is summed with -g in D dimensions.", 
   "Text"], Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"];\nFCClearScalarProducts[];\
\nScan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {q, k, p, r}];\nSPD[q] = 0; SPD[k] = 0; \
SPD[p] = 0; SPD[r] = 0;\nSPD[q, k] = sh/2; SPD[k, p] = -th/2; SPD[q, p] = \
-uh/2; SPD[p, r] = sh/2; SPD[k, r] = -uh/2; SPD[q, r] = -th/2;\nSP[q] = 0; \
SP[k] = 0; SP[p] = 0; SP[r] = 0;\nSP[q, k] = sh/2; SP[k, p] = -th/2; SP[q, p] \
= -uh/2; SP[p, r] = sh/2; SP[k, r] = -uh/2; SP[q, r] = -th/2;\ncircularPhoton \
= Contract[I LC[mu, nu, alpha, beta] FV[q, alpha] FV[k, beta]/(2 SP[q, \
k])];\nphotonStrings = {GAD[rho].(GSD[k] + GSD[q]).GA[mu], GA[mu].(GSD[k] - \
GSD[r]).GAD[rho]};\nphotonStringsBar = {GA[nu].(GSD[k] + GSD[q]).GAD[sigma], \
GAD[sigma].(GSD[k] - GSD[r]).GA[nu]};\nphotonTraces = \
Table[DiracTrace[GS[p].photonStrings[[i]].GS[k].GA[5].photonStringsBar[[j]]]/\
2, {i, 2}, {j, 2}];\nphotonInterference = \
Table[Factor[TrickMandelstam[Cancel[Together[Simplify[Contract[ExpandScalarPr\
oduct[Contract[\n  DiracSimplify[circularPhoton photonTraces[[i, j]], \
DiracTraceEvaluate -> True] (-MTD[rho, sigma])]]]]]], {sh, th, uh, 0}]], {i, \
2}, {j, 2}];\nphotonPolarized = CF ee^2 eq^2 gs^2 \
Factor[TrickMandelstam[Cancel[Together[\n  photonInterference[[1, 1]]/sh^2 + \
photonInterference[[2, 2]]/uh^2 + (photonInterference[[1, 2]] + \
photonInterference[[2, 1]])/(sh uh)]], {sh, th, uh, 0}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["photon = <|\"Unpolarized\" -> photonUnpolarized, \"Polarized\" -> \
photonPolarized|>;", "Input"], Cell["Save", "Section"], 
  Cell["Algebra.wl holds everything step 3 needs: the Born and photon squares \
(functions of D), the real squares (functions of D, a, b, s, t, u and spe3) \
and the virtual scalar family.", "Text"], Cell["algebra = <|\"Born\" -> born, \
\"Real\" -> real, \"Photon\" -> photon, \"VirtualFamily\" -> \
virtualFamily|>;\nSaveResult[\"Algebra\", algebra, \
\"FeynCalc\"];\nKeys[algebra]", "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
